! PlantLiquidITECooling.idf
!
! Basic file description:  This file demonstrates the use of the Coil:Cooling:ITE:ColdPlate object, which models a
!                          direct-to-chip (D2C) liquid cooling cold plate for liquid-cooled IT equipment.
!                          It is based on PlantLoadProfile.idf, but has been modified to also include a zone,
!                          taken from the one zone example files (e.g. 1ZoneDataCenterCRAC_wPumpedDXCoolingCoil.idf).
!
!                          This file is not intended to represent an actual data center. The building, loads, schedules,
!                          temperatures and equipment are simplified, and are only meant to exercise the cold plate object.
!
! Highlights:              The cold plate is on the demand side of a coolant distribution unit (CDU) loop, which
!                          circulates a 25% propylene glycol mixture (PG25, defined with FluidProperties:GlycolConcentration).
!                          The supply side of the CDU loop has a variable speed pump and a HeatExchanger:FluidToFluid,
!                          which connects the CDU loop to the Main Loop, a chilled water plant loop served by an
!                          air-cooled constant COP chiller. The chiller operates in ConstantFlow mode, so the Main Loop
!                          runs at a constant flow rate. Both loops are controlled to a 30 C supply temperature,
!                          which is typical of warm water cooling in liquid-cooled data centers.
!
!                          The IT equipment load is represented by a schedule (see the field IT Equipment Load Schedule Name),
!                          so no ElectricEquipment:ITE:LiquidCooled object is used. The cold plate has an availability
!                          schedule, and is only available between 08:00 and 20:00 on weekdays. Heat that is not removed by the
!                          coolant, which includes all of the load while the cold plate is unavailable, is added to the zone.
!                          The zone has no HVAC system, so its temperature floats.
!
!                          The flow rates of the cold plate are autosized, based on the Sizing:Plant objects, and the cold
!                          plate flow is variable to maintain the target case operating temperature.
!
!                          The thermal resistance modifier curve (Curve:Exponent) was obtained by fitting an exponent curve
!                          through data published in peer-reviewed sources. It is intended to represent a typical modification
!                          of the thermal resistance with the flow rate for the "Standard" thermal resistance approach.
!
! Simulation Location/Run: Miami Intl Ap FL USA WMO=722020, 2 design days, 1 run period.
!
! Design Days:             Miami Intl Ap FL USA Annual Heating 99.6%, MaxDB=8.7°C
!                          Miami Intl Ap FL USA Annual Cooling (DB=>MWB) .4%, MaxDB=33.2°C MWB=25.3°C
!
! Run Period (Weather File): Full annual simulation, USA_FL_Miami.Intl.AP.722020_TMY3.epw
!
! Run Control:             No zone or plant sizing calculations. The design days and the weather file run period are simulated.
!
! Building:                Fictional 1 zone building with resistive walls based on the 1ZoneUncontrolled example.
!                          No windows. No internal mass. The building is oriented due north.
!
! Floor Area:              232.26 m2
! Number of Stories:       1
!
! Plant:                   CDU loop (PG25): variable speed pump and heat exchanger on the supply side, cold plate on the
!                          demand side. Main Loop (water): constant flow chiller and pump on the supply side, heat exchanger
!                          on the demand side.

  Version,
    26.2;                    !- Version Identifier

  Building,
    Plant Load Profile Example,  !- Name
    0.0,                     !- North Axis {deg}
    Suburbs,                 !- Terrain
    0.04,                    !- Loads Convergence Tolerance Value {W}
    0.04,                    !- Temperature Convergence Tolerance Value {deltaC}
    FullInteriorAndExterior, !- Solar Distribution
    25,                      !- Maximum Number of Warmup Days
    6;                       !- Minimum Number of Warmup Days

  Timestep,
    6;                       !- Number of Timesteps per Hour

  Site:Location,
    Miami Intl Ap FL USA WMO=722020,  !- Name
    25.82,                   !- Latitude {deg}
    -80.30,                  !- Longitude {deg}
    -5.00,                   !- Time Zone {hr}
    11.00;                   !- Elevation {m}

 ! Miami Intl Ap Annual Cooling Design Conditions Wind Speed=4.5m/s Wind Dir=140
 ! Hottest Month=July
 ! Miami Intl Ap FL USA Annual Cooling (DB=>MWB) .4%, MaxDB=33.2°C MWB=25.3°C

  SizingPeriod:DesignDay,
    Miami Intl Ap Ann Clg .4% Condns DB=>MWB,  !- Name
    7,                       !- Month
    21,                      !- Day of Month
    SummerDesignDay,         !- Day Type
    33.2,                    !- Maximum Dry-Bulb Temperature {C}
    6.7,                     !- Daily Dry-Bulb Temperature Range {deltaC}
    ,                        !- Dry-Bulb Temperature Range Modifier Type
    ,                        !- Dry-Bulb Temperature Range Modifier Day Schedule Name
    Wetbulb,                 !- Humidity Condition Type
    25.3,                    !- Wetbulb or DewPoint at Maximum Dry-Bulb {C}
    ,                        !- Humidity Condition Day Schedule Name
    ,                        !- Humidity Ratio at Maximum Dry-Bulb {kgWater/kgDryAir}
    ,                        !- Enthalpy at Maximum Dry-Bulb {J/kg}
    ,                        !- Daily Wet-Bulb Temperature Range {deltaC}
    101217.,                 !- Barometric Pressure {Pa}
    4.5,                     !- Wind Speed {m/s}
    140,                     !- Wind Direction {deg}
    No,                      !- Rain Indicator
    No,                      !- Snow Indicator
    No,                      !- Daylight Saving Time Indicator
    ASHRAEClearSky,          !- Solar Model Indicator
    ,                        !- Beam Solar Day Schedule Name
    ,                        !- Diffuse Solar Day Schedule Name
    ,                        !- ASHRAE Clear Sky Optical Depth for Beam Irradiance (taub) {dimensionless}
    ,                        !- ASHRAE Clear Sky Optical Depth for Diffuse Irradiance (taud) {dimensionless}
    1.00;                    !- Sky Clearness

 ! Miami Intl Ap FL USA Annual Heating Design Conditions Wind Speed=3.8m/s Wind Dir=340
 ! Coldest Month=January
 ! Miami Intl Ap FL USA Annual Heating 99.6%, MaxDB=8.7°C

  SizingPeriod:DesignDay,
